  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the dog's howling action",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the dog howling, as the exaggerated text 'Goooooooooooooon!!!!' humorously represents the sound the dog is making. The user identifies with the dog's expressive, vocalized behavior, imagining themselves as the source of the howl or experiencing the sensation of howling in that context. This projection is implicit, not explicit (e.g., no 'you' or 'me' text), but is inferred from the meme format where the viewer is invited to imagine themselves in the dog's place or to relate to its exaggerated emotion.",
